From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 09:38:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 206/342] CodyCam: record video files (M45)

A "Record video" button under the picture records what the camera sends
into ~/Videos/CodyCam <date> <time>.mkv: Matroska with MPEG-4 video, the
size and frame rate of the connection (320x240 at 30), through the
Media Kit's writer and the FFmpeg plugin's encoder. The button turns
into "Stop recording"; the status line says where the file goes and,
when stopped, its length.

VideoRecorder copies each frame the consumer gets (also one too late to
be shown) and encodes in a thread of its own. The encoder counts
frames, so the recorder places them by their time: a frame is written
again for the frames it stands for, one that came early is left out,
and the video plays at the speed it was taken also when the camera
lowers its rate in low light (15 fps here). Quitting CodyCam while it
records finishes the file.

Tested with the C920: 12.3 s recorded as 371 frames at 30 fps (the
camera at 15), MediaPlayer plays it; quitting during a recording left a
whole file (8.5 s); the encoder takes about a quarter of a core.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
